  "body": "# Uninitialized `maturityTime` Mapping Allows Instant Withdrawals, Completely Bypassing Lock-up Mechanism\n\n## Severity\n**Medium**\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe `GaugeV2` contract implements a maturity check in the `_withdraw` function to enforce a time-based lock-up period before users can withdraw their deposited tokens:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _withdraw(uint256 amount) internal nonReentrant isNotEmergency updateReward(msg.sender) {\n    require(amount > 0, \"ZV\");\n    require(_balances[msg.sender] >= amount, \"INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE\");\n    require(_balanceOf(msg.sender) > 0, \"ZV\");\n    require(block.timestamp >= maturityTime[msg.sender], \"!MATURE\"); // ❌ Always passes\n    \n    // ... withdrawal logic\n}\n```\n\nHowever, the critical flaw is that the `maturityTime` mapping is **never initialized or updated** anywhere in the contract. In Solidity, uninitialized `uint256` mappings default to `0` for all keys. This means:\n\n- `maturityTime[user]` always equals `0` (Unix epoch: January 1, 1970)\n- `block.timestamp` in any real-world scenario is always greater than `0`\n- The condition `block.timestamp >= maturityTime[msg.sender]` **always evaluates to `true`**\n\nThe maturity check becomes a no-op, providing zero protection against immediate withdrawals.\n\n### Impact\n\nThis vulnerability has several significant impacts:\n\n1. **Complete Bypass of Lock-up Mechanism**: Users can deposit and immediately withdraw their tokens in the same transaction or block, rendering the intended maturity/vesting period completely useless.\n\n3. Users could potentially:\n   - Deposit tokens just before reward distribution\n   - Claim rewards\n   - Immediately withdraw without any lock-up penalty\n   - This enables \"flash-staking\" attacks on the reward system\n\n4. **Protocol Design Failure**: The presence of unused maturity tracking code suggests the protocol intended to implement time-locked staking but failed to complete the implementation, leaving a security gap.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\n### Implement Proper Maturity Initialization\n\n\n```solidity\nuint256 public constant LOCK_DURATION = 7 days; \n\nfunction _deposit(uint256 amount) internal nonReentrant isNotEmergency updateReward(msg.sender) {\n    require(amount > 0, \"ZV\");\n    \n    TOKEN.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n    _totalSupply = _totalSupply + amount;\n    _balances[msg.sender] = _balances[msg.sender] + amount;\n    \n    // ✅ Initialize maturity time on deposit\n    if (maturityTime[msg.sender] == 0) {\n        maturityTime[msg.sender] = block.timestamp + LOCK_DURATION;\n    } else {\n        // Extend maturity if user deposits again\n        maturityTime[msg.sender] = block.timestamp + LOCK_DURATION;\n    }\n    \n    if (address(gaugeRewarder) != address(0)) {\n        IRewarder(gaugeRewarder).onReward(msg.sender, msg.sender, _balanceOf(msg.sender));\n    }\n    \n    emit Deposit(msg.sender, amount);\n}\n```\n\n**Alternative approach with flexible lock periods:**\n\n```solidity\nmapping(address => uint256) public userLockDuration;\n\nfunction depositWithLock(uint256 amount, uint256 lockDuration) external {\n    require(lockDuration >= MIN_LOCK && lockDuration <= MAX_LOCK, \"Invalid lock\");\n    userLockDuration[msg.sender] = lockDuration;\n    maturityTime[msg.sender] = block.timestamp + lockDuration;\n    _deposit(amount);\n}\n```",
